  "description": "<div>\n  <p>Turn <code>beginWord</code> into <code>endWord</code> by replacing exactly one letter per step. Every word after the first must occur in <code>wordList</code>. Return the fewest words in such a sequence, counting both endpoints, or zero if no sequence exists.</p>\n  <p>A one-letter change may pass through words not closer to the target; find the shortest valid chain.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> beginWord = &quot;hit&quot;, endWord = &quot;cog&quot;, wordList = [&quot;hot&quot;,&quot;dot&quot;,&quot;dog&quot;,&quot;lot&quot;,&quot;log&quot;,&quot;cog&quot;]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 5</pre>\n  <p>One shortest chain is hit→hot→dot→dog→cog.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> beginWord = &quot;hit&quot;, endWord = &quot;cog&quot;, wordList = [&quot;hot&quot;,&quot;dot&quot;,&quot;dog&quot;,&quot;lot&quot;,&quot;log&quot;]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 0</pre>\n  <p>The target is missing from the permitted words.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> beginWord = &quot;a&quot;, endWord = &quot;c&quot;, wordList = [&quot;a&quot;,&quot;b&quot;,&quot;c&quot;]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 2</pre>\n  <p>Changing a to c takes one step, making two words.</p>\n  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><code>1 &lt;= beginWord.length = endWord.length &lt;= 10</code>.</li>\n    <li><code>0 &lt;= wordList.length &lt;= 100</code>; all words have the same length, use lowercase English letters, and are distinct.</li>\n    <li><code>beginWord</code> need not be in the list; when the two endpoints are equal return <code>1</code>.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>",
